\question \emph{Section 1.5, Exercise 12}

Determine which of the following formulas are equivalent:

\[
\begin{aligned}
(a)&\quad P\to(Q\to R),\\
(b)&\quad Q\to(P\to R),\\
(c)&\quad (P\to Q)\land(P\to R),\\
(d)&\quad (P\land Q)\to R,\\
(e)&\quad P\to(Q\land R).
\end{aligned}
\]

First simplify each formula.

For (a),
\[
\begin{aligned}
P\to(Q\to R)
&\equiv \neg P\lor(\neg Q\lor R)\\
&\equiv \neg P\lor\neg Q\lor R.
\end{aligned}
\]

For (b),
\[
\begin{aligned}
Q\to(P\to R)
&\equiv \neg Q\lor(\neg P\lor R)\\
&\equiv \neg P\lor\neg Q\lor R.
\end{aligned}
\]

For (c),
\[
\begin{aligned}
(P\to Q)\land(P\to R)
&\equiv(\neg P\lor Q)\land(\neg P\lor R)\\
&\equiv\neg P\lor(Q\land R).
\end{aligned}
\]
This is equivalent to (e).

For (d),
\[
(P\land Q)\to R
\equiv\neg(P\land Q)\lor R
\equiv\neg P\lor\neg Q\lor R.
\]

For (e),
\[
P\to(Q\land R)
\equiv\neg P\lor(Q\land R).
\]

Thus,
\[
\boxed{(a)\equiv(b)\equiv(d)}
\]
and
\[
\boxed{(c)\equiv(e)}.
\]

The two groups are not equivalent to each other.

